# diff
# Betaflight / SITL (SITL) 4.5.1
#
# AIR65 II RACING. BetaFPV's own factory tune for the Air65 II Racing, the
# 30000 kV variant on the same GF1207 three blade. Brass bushings instead of
# the Champion's dual ball bearings and the heavier Air65 II frame, so 17.7 g
# dry against 16.6, and a motor that trades top end for throttle response.
#
# PROVENANCE. Taken from "A65 II R_0702_Racing_GF 1207_2026_6_0
# 20260520.txt", the CLI BetaFPV publishes for this aircraft at
# support.betafpv.com/hc/en-us/articles/54654422544409 (attachment
# 58300189265433). Betaflight 2026.6.0-alpha on a BETAFPVG473_V2 board;
# every PID, filter, TPA and idle value below is copied from it verbatim.
#
# AGAINST THE CHAMPION: every gain is higher, because
# simplified_master_multiplier is 85 rather than 75, and D is relatively
# higher still (simplified_d_gain 105 against 95) while I is lower (80
# against 95). That is the shape of a tune for a motor with less authority:
# more damping, less integral, and the TPA breakpoint 30 counts further up
# the stick at 1210 because a 30000 kV motor sags a little less.
#
# WHAT A WHOOP TUNE LOOKS LIKE, because it is not what the folklore says.
# The received wisdom is that whoops run high P and low D. This one runs
# roll P33 D21 F40 against Betaflight 4.5.1's 5 inch default of P45 D40
# F120: P, D AND feedforward are all well below stock, because
# simplified_master_multiplier is 75. A 23 g machine with three times a
# 5 inch's angular acceleration does not need the gain. What IS whoop
# specific is the shape:
#
#   * D is 68 percent of P against the 5 inch default's 89. There is almost
#     no propwash to damp and the rotor inertia is a millionth of a 5 inch's.
#   * d_max_gain is 20 against a default of 37, and d_max sits at about 110
#     percent of D. The D boost band is deliberately narrow.
#   * tpa_breakpoint is 1210 against a default of 1350. THIS is the clearest
#     "because it is 1S" decision in the whole file. The pack sags 4.2 V to
#     3.2 V under a punch, a 23 percent collapse where a 6S race pack loses
#     8, so the gains have to start coming off a fifth of the way up the
#     stick instead of two thirds.
#   * throttle_boost is 0. Every BetaFPV whoop dump sets it there; the 4.5.1
#     default is 5.
#   * dyn_idle_min_rpm 30, which is 3000 rpm, against a hover of 34,480.
#
# NO RATES, following configs/registry.js. BetaFPV ships this aircraft on
# ACTUAL rates with srate 58 / 58 / 50, which is 580 deg/s on roll and pitch
# and 500 on yaw: a RACING whoop flies SLOWER rates than a 5 inch freestyle
# quad, because the track is three metres wide. Those are the numbers the
# shell's whoop default carries; see configs/rates.js. To fly them exactly,
# set 580 max and 0 expo in Settings.
#
